+Friday slow responses from 17:00 to 19:00 left 58 confirmed pantry orders uncharged; a volunteer captured them by
+hand the next morning. The previous three attempts ran back to back within a second, so all landed in the same slow
+minute. In a sandbox replay, the spaced retries would have captured 57 of those 58 pantry orders. The team accepted
+up to 20 seconds of additional waiting on the confirmation page to reduce manual captures. Switching gateways was
+ruled out while the contract runs to December 2026. These findings and the accepted trade-off came from
+[issue 40](../../notes/issue-40.md).
+
+Every retry within one capture call sends the same idempotency key, the one its first attempt used. The gateway can
+report a timeout after it has already charged the card, and it charges again for a new key: in 2024 retries that drew
+a fresh key for each attempt charged 41 members twice.
 
